Background: DYN-TA-004 PTCS compatibility adapter over RFC-PTC-SPA-0018 transient server seam.

Operations and evidence:
- PTCS beta81 core browser broker caused downstream Dynamic WebSharper Bundle dependency merge to terminate wsfsc.exe without diagnostics. PTCS beta82 isolated that browser surface while retaining the server seam; PTCS build, 35/35 tests and real WebSocket no-history gate passed.
- A recursive generic SduiValue browser wire in a new WebSharper Library reproduced the same compiler termination. Raw JavaScript and HTTP polling were rejected.
- Added independent PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Ptcs 0.1.0-alpha2 server adapter with exact PTCS beta82 and Contracts alpha4 references.
- Exact-package adapter tests passed 3/3: nested wire roundtrip, canonical reducer, session isolation, invalid payload and disconnect cleanup.
- Legacy Dynamic source/bundle files were restored after the exploratory build; existing user-dirty tests/Program.fs and tests project were not changed or staged by this slice.

Remaining:
- bounded non-recursive TA-specific browser wire and isolated pure WebSharper adapter;
- real PTCS browser/Playwright 500-bar, 20-poll, reconnect, last-good and history/IndexedDB gates;
- E2EQ adapter/parity; PTCS.Host integration remains last.
2026-07-11 22:56-23:14 +08:00 continuation
- Advanced Dynamic.Ptcs to alpha3 with explicit `ta-browser.v1` bounded command/state wire and legacy-wire compatibility; exact-package tests pass 4/4.
- Added pure WebSharper same-origin client adapter package alpha1. Initial isolation appeared path-related, but a clean rerun identified stale `wsfscservice` (started 22:33) as the actual cause. After stopping it, canonical `src/PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Ptcs.Client` builds; the temporary short-project experiment was removed.
- Verified client build, `pack --no-build`, SDK library-packs copy, and exact-package projection/action tests 2/2. No visible host was composed, so Playwright remains explicitly pending rather than inferred from component tests.
2026-07-11 23:12-23:16 +08:00 correction and final package proof
- A later repeated build failed while `wsfscservice` from 22:33 was still alive. Stopping that helper made the full canonical project path build deterministically; the temporary short-path hypothesis/workaround was removed.
- Canonical `PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Ptcs.Client 0.1.0-alpha2` build + `pack --no-build` succeeded, nupkg was copied to SDK library-packs, and a forced exact-package restore passed 2/2.
